{"contentHash":"5c94c31640c678f9a934a0fec90954448d7bc4a8bcbdbe2aa1e969bf1b2b637f","path":"apps/borso-fr/site/src/12-travaux/main.tsx","ledgerHash":"c9cc14decde46c91990639a64998fea47f78ae890f43c022107f6ddd99ee7fd2","reviewer":"standards-reviewer","sealedAt":"2026-08-20T10:01:41.650Z","note":"Entry points gaining installWarpDrive(). Both read in full. Both carry @FollowsBlueprint site-entrypoint and hold to it: side-effect imports, one install call, then one mount of one tree, with the missing root thrown rather than swallowed. Bare installWarpDrive() takes the PAGE_FADE_DURATION_MILLISECONDS default of 420 ms (warp-jump.core.ts:26, warp-drive.ts:71), which is the number each page's fade reads back as --transition-hold (12-travaux/index.html:22, art/mondrian/index.html:17,21) — so the hold and the fade are one number, as the Fade entry in VOCABULARY.md claims. No prose comment in either file, so nothing to restate; no boolean is negated; no disable comment; no effect; no hand-written mirror type; nothing renders here, so the 375-pixel bullet has no subject."}
{"contentHash":"b9d7950f59fb6c1c0ff81401ab5692be7ced1d9ded3d653262513817fb7ac6f8","path":"apps/borso-fr/site/src/art/mondrian/App.tsx","ledgerHash":"c9cc14decde46c91990639a64998fea47f78ae890f43c022107f6ddd99ee7fd2","reviewer":"standards-reviewer","sealedAt":"2026-08-19T18:12:00.887Z","note":"Lightspeed jump on borso-fr, read in full. Both surviving effects name the external system they synchronise with (ogl WebGL renderer, requestAnimationFrame). getElementById and getDialogById in home-page.ts throw when the element is absent, which is what the get verb promises. warp-jump.core.ts is the one file of this change left unsealed."}
