{"contentHash":"d06dddec2e9145a6b7c2ab2825021d761091f7932937605e234003db7f4509e4","path":"apps/borso-fr/site/src/warp/warp-jump.core.ts","ledgerHash":"c9cc14decde46c91990639a64998fea47f78ae890f43c022107f6ddd99ee7fd2","reviewer":"standards-reviewer","sealedAt":"2026-08-20T08:37:07.853Z","note":"Sealed on the second read of this session. The first read carried a sentence on selectJumpProgress reading 'There is no ceiling at the end of the jump, only the one at HIGHEST_PROGRESS, which is what lets the field keep building while the destination is still loading' — an absence description of the clamp at 1 this revision dropped, and a restatement of the HIGHEST_PROGRESS JSDoc. It was removed while the review was open and this seal is on the content without it. Both documented numbers were checked against the stated cruising rate of 0.036 cycles a second: 200 gives 7.2 cycles a second and 8.3 frames a crossing at 60 Hz, HIGHEST_PROGRESS 1.6 gives 319.4x, 11.5 cycles a second and 5.2 frames, and sqrt(1.6) is 1.26 of the jump duration, which is the 'quarter again' the comment claims. Pure, time enters as an argument, every literal named."}
{"contentHash":"d06dddec2e9145a6b7c2ab2825021d761091f7932937605e234003db7f4509e4","path":"apps/borso-fr/site/src/warp/warp-jump.core.ts","ledgerHash":"c9cc14decde46c91990639a64998fea47f78ae890f43c022107f6ddd99ee7fd2","reviewer":"standards-reviewer","sealedAt":"2026-08-20T08:38:49.523Z","note":"Re-read in full after the 08:35 finding was fixed: the sentence on the absent clamp is gone and the surviving floor comment states only why Math.max(...,0) is there. Every numeric comment re-derived against source rather than the prior report - main.tsx:10,13 give starSpeed 0.3 and speed 1.2, galaxy-clock.core.ts:41 divides by STAR_SPEED_DIVISOR 10, and galaxy-shaders.ts:169 cycles depth on uStarSpeed*uSpeed, so cruising is 0.036 cycles/s (28 s a crossing), 200 gives 7.2 c/s (8.3 frames at 60 Hz) and HIGHEST_PROGRESS 1.6 gives 11.5 c/s (5.2 frames) at sqrt(1.6)=1.26 of the jump. select* verbs all return; no booleans, no effects, no clock read - now arrives as an argument."}
{"contentHash":"e99b49c88e775bb96f30a7cb294dddd97c1eaf39861a5b313b2ed50379844da8","path":"apps/borso-fr/site/src/warp/warp-jump.core.ts","ledgerHash":"c9cc14decde46c91990639a64998fea47f78ae890f43c022107f6ddd99ee7fd2","reviewer":"standards-reviewer","sealedAt":"2026-08-20T08:44:20.944Z","note":"Re-read in full at working-tree content after the TOP_STAR_SPEED_MULTIPLIER comment change. Every arithmetic claim in the comments verified against source: 0.036 cycles/s is starSpeed 0.3 / 10 * speed 1.2 from main.tsx and STAR_SPEED_DIVISOR in galaxy-clock.core.ts; 200 gives 7.2 cycles/s, 0.14 s, eight frames at 60 Hz; HIGHEST_PROGRESS 1.6 gives 319.4x, 0.087 s, five frames, reached at sqrt(1.6)=1.26 of the jump. The new claim that the sibling test pins the constant is true: warp-jump.core.test.ts hard-codes 200 or 199 on lines 23, 33, 37, 44, 50, 61. select verbs match the 01 table, file is pure, now arrives as a parameter."}
